// A module whose body starts past instruction 1023.
//
// OP_NEW used to carry the entry point itself, in ten bits, as an ABSOLUTE
// index into the instruction stream. Anything past 1023 wrapped: a module whose
// ENTER sat at 1557 was called at 533, straight into unrelated code. Nothing
// reported it -- no error, no wrong return value, the object simply produced
// nothing, and only a program long enough to reach the wrap could show it.
//
// The entry point comes from the module DECLARATION now, where it is a full
// index_t. The padding below is what makes this test a test: it exists to push
// the module past the old ceiling, so shortening it silently retires the check.
//
// 180 pairs is ~1500 instructions with the OP_SEGMENT runs that carry the names.
#variable Pad000 = 0
Pad000 = Pad000 + 1
#variable Pad001 = 1
Pad001 = Pad001 + 1
#variable Pad002 = 2
Pad002 = Pad002 + 1
#variable Pad003 = 3
Pad003 = Pad003 + 1
